title: CLI ignores $ENV{KUBECONFIG}
updated: 2026-08-13T05:14:37Z
---

Kubernetes::REST::Kubeconfig defaults its kubeconfig_path to $ENV{KUBECONFIG} // "$ENV{HOME}/.kube/config" (Kubeconfig.pm:68), but CLI::Role::Connection declares its own --kubeconfig option with default => sub { "$ENV{HOME}/.kube/config" } and always passes that value on. The option is therefore never undef, Kubeconfig never reaches its own default, and $ENV{KUBECONFIG} is ignored by both kube_client and kube_watch -- while every other tool in the ecosystem honours it.

Fix is to let the option default to undef and only pass kubeconfig_path when it is set, so Kubeconfig applies its own precedence. bin/kube_client POD ENVIRONMENT should then list KUBECONFIG.

Side effect of the same line: with HOME unset the default interpolates an undef and warns.

Found while doing #5/#6; Role/Connection.pm was outside that ticket scope.
